t you appeared in in the debate  the other night you appeared to have a  kind of a non-aggression pact with  Elizabeth Warren do you two have a deal  - not to attack each other at least at  this stage look Elizabeth and I have  been friends for over 20 years she's  running hard campaign and I'm running my  campaign they're different campaigns  what do you want I think the most I  think the most effective way to campaign  to be honest with you is to talk to the  American people about the why the middle  class is disappearing why we have  massive income and wealth inequality the  nature the great challenge we face in  terms of climate change the thievery  that it's now going on within the  pharmaceutical industry where there is  literally price fix  but there is just incredible greed you  talk about those issues you do well you  try to beat up on somebody else frankly  I don't think it's good politics so it's  senator at some point you and Elizabeth  Warren as most pundits seem to indicate  will make that that next debate how will  you differentiate yourself from her you  to progressives I'll tell you I'll let  you guys and the pundit tree and the  American people make that decision all  principle there what is the biggest  difference between you and senator  Sanders senator no no I have no I have  to tell the American people what I  believe and I'm gonna take on the greed  of Wall Street the drug companies the  insurance companies we are gonna tell  the fossil fuel industry that they  cannot continue to destroy this planet  for their short-term profits right now  the American people understand there is  something wrong when people are many  people are working longer hours for  lower wages 49% of all new income goes  to the top one percent that's my message  the American people we got to take on  corporate greed we got to create an  economy that works for all of us not  just the 1% that's my message that's  what I can't paint on all right senator  Sanders thank you so